00:41:30.129 --> 00:41:31.962
Played by me.

509
00:41:31.964 --> 00:41:35.900
His child bride
has a son in his absence.

510
00:41:35.902 --> 00:41:40.105
When he returns home,
he has new wife.

511
00:41:40.107 --> 00:41:42.877
The child bride is devastated.

512
00:41:44.143 --> 00:41:46.777
He realizes he has made
a terrible mistake,

513
00:41:46.779 --> 00:41:50.984
but he's too much
of a coward to face her.

514
00:41:51.917 --> 00:41:53.153
Does she forgive him?

515
00:41:54.453 --> 00:41:57.955
No. She kills herself.

516
00:41:57.957 --> 00:41:59.125
Depressing.

517
00:41:59.926 --> 00:42:01.761
Ah, it's opera.

518
00:42:12.205 --> 00:42:16.043
When I was little,
I caught my mum with someone.

519
00:42:19.111 --> 00:42:20.380
I didn't know him.

520
00:42:21.314 --> 00:42:22.917
And I never told my dad.

521
00:42:24.151 --> 00:42:25.386
But I didn't have to.

522
00:42:27.988 --> 00:42:29.723
A week later, he was gone.

523
00:42:31.825 --> 00:42:34.928
No note, no good-bye, nothing.

524
00:42:39.399 --> 00:42:41.469
A house is expensive to keep.

525
00:42:42.368 --> 00:42:44.104
Things break all the time.

526
00:42:45.038 --> 00:42:46.841
There's land,
and animals, and...

527
00:42:48.408 --> 00:42:50.277
She refuses to leave...

528
00:42:53.113 --> 00:42:55.116
because she thinks
he's coming back.

529
00:42:58.518 --> 00:43:00.154
He's not coming back.

530
00:43:01.187 --> 00:43:02.522
I know that now.

531
00:43:07.294 --> 00:43:08.895
Sorry about the other night.

532
00:43:09.596 --> 00:43:10.998
It's okay.

533
00:43:11.897 --> 00:43:13.334
You were disappointed.

534
00:43:15.035 --> 00:43:17.937
But I'm not
going to let you give up.

535
00:43:19.105 --> 00:43:21.075
I wasted my own talent.

536
00:43:22.341 --> 00:43:25.845
Maybe you're
my second chance to...

537
00:43:27.279 --> 00:43:28.848
be useful now.

538
00:43:30.917 --> 00:43:32.119
Well, that's good.

539
00:43:33.252 --> 00:43:34.821
Because I've got some news.

540
00:43:40.393 --> 00:43:42.463
You're wasting your time,
we can't pay you.

541
00:43:43.462 --> 00:43:44.998
Yes, this is Violet.

542
00:43:46.366 --> 00:43:48.068
They made a mistake.

543
00:43:49.402 --> 00:43:51.205
The girl who won my group...

544
00:43:53.172 --> 00:43:55.176
she was using a fake name.

545
00:43:57.243 --> 00:44:01.212
Turns out she'd already entered
another competition before.

546
00:44:05.919 --> 00:44:07.555
She's been disqualified.

547
00:44:19.299 --> 00:44:21.235
We're going to London, Vlad.

548
00:44:24.203 --> 00:44:25.573
Going to the finals.

549
00:44:26.973 --> 00:44:29.143
Wow.

550
00:44:35.649 --> 00:44:37.415
Here we are
on the Isle of Wight,

551
00:44:37.417 --> 00:44:40.451
a small but picturesque island
off the coast of England.

552
00:44:40.453 --> 00:44:44.455
And behind me,
the home of Violet Valenski,

553
00:44:44.457 --> 00:44:48.125
the first contestant from the island
to make the Teen Spirit finals.

554
00:44:48.127 --> 00:44:50.194
I never dreamed
I would make it this far.

555
00:44:50.196 --> 00:44:55.302
I keep waiting for them to call
back and say there's been a mistake.

556
00:44:59.138 --> 00:45:01.239
The competition, which provides
a platform for young British talent,

557
00:45:01.241 --> 00:45:02.674
has surged in popularity

558
00:45:02.676 --> 00:45:04.275
thanks to
high-profile contestants

559
00:45:04.277 --> 00:45:06.678
like Keyan Spears
and Three Two Tango.

560
00:45:09.181 --> 00:45:10.614
Violet, who lives alone
with her mother,

561
00:45:10.616 --> 00:45:13.150
has no expectations
of the same success,

562
00:45:13.152 --> 00:45:16.120
but looks forward to performing
on a global stage.

563
00:45:16.122 --> 00:45:17.955
I know I'm not
the best singer in England,

564
00:45:17.957 --> 00:45:19.690
but I'm gonna try to work
really hard to be a better one

565
00:45:19.692 --> 00:45:22.092
by the time we get to London.

566
00:45:22.094 --> 00:45:24.127
And forgive the question,

567
00:45:24.129 --> 00:45:26.297
but we have to ask,

568
00:45:26.299 --> 00:45:27.998
is there a special someone in your life?

569
00:45:28.000 --> 00:45:29.335
<i>No special someone.</i>

570
00:45:30.136 --> 00:45:31.372
<i>I don't believe in love.</i>

571
00:45:32.071 --> 00:45:33.339
Love's not real.

572
00:45:34.607 --> 00:45:40.511
<i>♪ I look up
To the little bird ♪</i>

573
00:45:40.513 --> 00:45:46.953
<i>♪ That glides across the sky ♪</i>

574
00:45:49.288 --> 00:45:55.993
<i>♪ He sings
The clearest melody ♪</i>

575
00:45:55.995 --> 00:46:02.368
<i>♪ It makes me want to cry ♪</i>

576
00:46:03.703 --> 00:46:07.538
<i>♪ It makes me want
To sit right down ♪</i>

577
00:46:07.540 --> 00:46:11.277
<i>♪ And cry, cry, cry, yeah ♪</i>

578
00:46:12.578 --> 00:46:18.783
<i>♪ I walk along
The city streets ♪</i>

579
00:46:18.785 --> 00:46:25.292
<i>♪ So dark with rage and fear ♪</i>

580
00:46:26.426 --> 00:46:28.192
<i>♪ And I ♪</i>

581
00:46:28.194 --> 00:46:34.132
<i>♪ I wish
That I could be that bird ♪</i>

582
00:46:34.134 --> 00:46:40.474
<i>♪ And fly away from here ♪</i>

583
00:46:42.042 --> 00:46:44.775
<i>♪ I wish I had the wings ♪</i>

584
00:46:44.777 --> 00:46:50.114
<i>♪ To fly away from here
Yeah ♪</i>

585
00:46:50.116 --> 00:46:53.817
<i>♪ But, my, my, I feel so low ♪</i>

586
00:46:53.819 --> 00:46:57.721
<i>♪ My, my, where do I go? ♪</i>

587
00:46:57.723 --> 00:47:01.625
<i>♪ My, my, what do I know? ♪</i>

588
00:47:01.627 --> 00:47:05.495
<i>♪ My, my
We reap what we sow ♪</i>

589
00:47:05.497 --> 00:47:08.498
<i>♪ They always said
That you knew best ♪</i>

590
00:47:08.500 --> 00:47:10.768
<i>♪ But this little bird's ♪</i>

591
00:47:10.770 --> 00:47:13.404
<i>♪ Fallen out of that nest
Now ♪</i>

592
00:47:13.406 --> 00:47:15.138
<i>♪ I've got a feeling ♪</i>

593
00:47:15.140 --> 00:47:16.540
<i>♪ That it might have
Been blessed ♪</i>

594
00:47:16.542 --> 00:47:18.676
<i>♪ So I've just got to ♪</i>

595
00:47:18.678 --> 00:47:22.813
<i>♪ Put these wings to test ♪</i>

596
00:47:22.815 --> 00:47:26.616
Basically, Violet found out she got in
the final and needed a backing band.

597
00:47:26.618 --> 00:47:28.453
So, we were like, "Yes."

598
00:47:28.455 --> 00:47:30.620
And then we found out we had
to pay for our accommodation,

599
00:47:30.622 --> 00:47:32.522
so we were like, "No."

600
00:47:32.524 --> 00:47:34.525
And then Luke said he'd pay for
it, so we said yes again.

601
00:47:34.527 --> 00:47:35.859
No, I...

602
00:47:35.861 --> 00:47:37.230
No, I didn't.

603
00:47:37.797 --> 00:47:39.297
I'm not paying for it.

604
00:47:39.299 --> 00:47:40.730
Who is then?

605
00:47:40.732 --> 00:47:42.266
My mum's paying for it.

606
00:47:42.268 --> 00:47:43.567
May the Lord be with you.

607
00:47:43.569 --> 00:47:45.402
And with thy spirit.

608
00:47:45.404 --> 00:47:46.837
Thanks be to God.

609
00:47:46.839 --> 00:47:50.540
Before you go,
this is a special occasion.

610
00:47:50.542 --> 00:47:56.279
For one of our angels
has been blessed with a gift.

611
00:47:56.281 --> 00:48:02.587
May her faith and spirit give her
the strength to overcome temptation,

612
00:48:02.589 --> 00:48:05.759
and lead her
on the path to prosperity.

613
00:48:07.127 --> 00:48:09.296
- Amen.
- Amen.

614
00:48:15.801 --> 00:48:17.734
- Hey.
- Hey.

615
00:48:17.736 --> 00:48:20.406
- You didn't have to do that.
- It's not for you.

616
00:48:21.341 --> 00:48:23.210
Ma, Vlad's here.

617
00:48:28.314 --> 00:48:29.482
It's for you.

618
00:48:30.582 --> 00:48:32.118
That's very...

619
00:48:32.852 --> 00:48:34.221
unexpected.

620
00:48:36.288 --> 00:48:39.459
A woman like you should
get flowers every day.

621
00:48:40.259 --> 00:48:42.192
It's still 15 percent.

622
00:48:42.194 --> 00:48:43.794
All right...

623
00:48:45.431 --> 00:48:47.464
We should hit the road.

624
00:48:47.466 --> 00:48:49.866
Should I help with your bags?

625
00:48:49.868 --> 00:48:52.703
They... They're, um...
They're upstairs.

626
00:48:52.705 --> 00:48:53.873
- Yeah.
- Thanks.

627
00:48:54.674 --> 00:48:56.243
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

628
00:48:58.210 --> 00:48:59.413
I got you something.

629
00:49:00.312 --> 00:49:02.279
So I know you're safe.

630
00:49:02.281 --> 00:49:04.348
There's some credit on it.

631
00:49:04.350 --> 00:49:06.853
It will be cheaper than
using the phone at the hotel.

632
00:49:07.786 --> 00:49:09.453
I'll call
as soon as I get there.

633
00:49:09.455 --> 00:49:10.491
Good.

634
00:49:51.598 --> 00:49:54.401
We are going for four days.

635
00:50:13.518 --> 00:50:17.721
There's this train in London,
the Eurostar,

636
00:50:17.723 --> 00:50:19.759
it goes from London
to Paris direct.

637
00:50:20.960 --> 00:50:21.962
Ah...

638
00:50:22.828 --> 00:50:24.797
Paris is expensive.

639
00:50:25.797 --> 00:50:27.533
Not if we make our millions.

640
00:50:29.602 --> 00:50:30.971
Your daughter's there, no?

641
00:50:34.741 --> 00:50:36.810
You should visit her
after the finals.

642
00:51:08.073 --> 00:51:09.607
Miss Valenski.

643
00:51:09.609 --> 00:51:11.375
- Hi.
- Welcome to London.

644
00:51:11.377 --> 00:51:13.009
My name is Yuriy.

645
00:51:13.011 --> 00:51:15.281
I'll be taking care of you
over the next few days.

646
00:51:15.915 --> 00:51:16.880
This is Vlad.

647
00:51:16.882 --> 00:51:18.348
Hey, I'm manager.

648
00:51:18.350 --> 00:51:19.650
Vlad, a pleasure.

649
00:51:19.652 --> 00:51:21.986
That's our band,
Louise, Luke, Rollo.

650
00:51:21.988 --> 00:51:24.754
The band will have to
check in on the lower level.

651
00:51:24.756 --> 00:51:26.325
Sam will show you.

652
00:51:27.460 --> 00:51:29.060
Okay, bye.

653
00:51:29.062 --> 00:51:30.361
Luke.

654
00:51:30.363 --> 00:51:31.728
Luke, you are in charge, yeah?

655
00:51:31.730 --> 00:51:33.330
- Nothing from the minibar.
- Yeah, okay.

656
00:51:33.332 --> 00:51:35.866
- Hey, I'll be checking, yeah.
- Yes, okay.

657
00:51:35.868 --> 00:51:38.005
Violet, Vlad,
if you'd like to follow me.

658
00:51:47.779 --> 00:51:49.013
This room's for me?

659
00:51:49.015 --> 00:51:51.082
Yes, of course.

660
00:51:51.084 --> 00:51:53.683
Mr. Brajkovic,
we have you right next door.

661
00:51:53.685 --> 00:51:54.919
Good.

662
00:51:54.921 --> 00:51:57.420
This is your itinerary
for the weekend.

663
00:51:57.422 --> 00:51:58.955
You have about 30 minutes

664
00:51:58.957 --> 00:52:01.926
and then I will meet on
the conference room on level B.

665
00:52:01.928 --> 00:52:02.993
I can take it.

666
00:52:02.995 --> 00:52:04.661
Very good.

667
00:52:04.663 --> 00:52:06.797
I'll let you get settled
and meet you downstairs.

668
00:52:06.799 --> 00:52:07.968
Thank you.

669
00:52:13.439 --> 00:52:17.607
Mm. You have to do
a television promo.

670
00:52:17.609 --> 00:52:19.109
What for?

671
00:52:19.111 --> 00:52:20.777
For the broadcast
on Sunday.

672
00:52:20.779 --> 00:52:22.515
Everybody has to do it.

673
00:52:23.982 --> 00:52:27.384
It's nothing,
just say your name and, uh...

674
00:52:27.386 --> 00:52:29.422
where you are from, or...

675
00:52:31.790 --> 00:52:33.660
What do you want to wear?

676
00:52:35.527 --> 00:52:36.763
I'll wear this.

677
00:52:39.698 --> 00:52:43.100
Hey, we're The Shades.
Vote for us tomorrow on Teen Spirit.

678
00:52:43.102 --> 00:52:46.437
Hi, I'm Thomas King.
Vote for me tomorrow on Teen Spirit.

679
00:52:46.439 --> 00:52:50.009
Hi, I'm Violet, and you can vote for
me tomorrow night on Teen Spirit.

680
00:52:51.511 --> 00:52:55.745
Hi, we're Peckham Rose.
Vote for us tomorrow on Teen Spirit.

681
00:52:55.747 --> 00:52:59.852
I'm Roxy. You can vote for me
tomorrow night on Teen Spirit.

682
00:53:50.837 --> 00:53:53.103
Holy shit,
this is massive.

683
00:53:53.105 --> 00:53:54.541
Yeah.

684
00:53:56.576 --> 00:53:58.241
Oi, it's that foxy Roxy.

685
00:53:58.243 --> 00:54:00.780
- Yeah.
- Yeah, she's fit.

686
00:54:01.948 --> 00:54:04.114
Nah.
No, she's not my type.

687
00:54:06.585 --> 00:54:09.487
- What?
- Shut up.

688
00:54:09.489 --> 00:54:11.788
- And a side of chips.
<i>- Told ya. He's not good enough for you.</i>

689
00:54:11.790 --> 00:54:14.861
Mm-hmm.
Okay, thank you.

690
00:54:18.029 --> 00:54:20.029
<i>That doesn't make you
any less strong.</i>

691
00:54:20.031 --> 00:54:21.866
<i>To have somebody
care about ya.</i>

692
00:54:21.868 --> 00:54:25.002
<i>I know that you care.
I just want you to care less.</i>

693
00:54:25.004 --> 00:54:28.906
<i>Ever since Mum's died all you've been
doing is just taking it out on me.</i>

694
00:54:30.109 --> 00:54:31.107
<i>You're gonna set me off now.</i>

695
00:54:31.109 --> 00:54:32.511
That was quick.

696
00:54:33.011 --> 00:54:34.612
Hmm, housekeeper.

697
00:54:34.614 --> 00:54:36.216
Hmm. They came already.

698
00:54:38.017 --> 00:54:39.986
<i>I know
I'm not the perfect dad...</i>

699
00:54:44.991 --> 00:54:47.060
Uh... Can I help you?

700
00:55:00.138 --> 00:55:03.207
Everybody
seems to have no clothes on at all.

701
00:55:03.209 --> 00:55:05.174
Why is it that all
of the stories you tell me...

702
00:55:05.176 --> 00:55:09.013
I know. I have absolutely no...
Ooh, hang on.

703
00:55:09.015 --> 00:55:11.618
This one... This one is for later.

704
00:55:12.151 --> 00:55:14.217
Hi, hi!

705
00:55:14.219 --> 00:55:16.754
Uh, Alexa's being an idiot.
Ignore her.

706
00:55:16.756 --> 00:55:18.254
Everyone...

707
00:55:18.256 --> 00:55:19.790
this is Violet.

708
00:55:19.792 --> 00:55:22.859
- And, uh, Mr...
- Brajkovic.

709
00:55:22.861 --> 00:55:24.597
Jules. Hi.

710
00:55:26.098 --> 00:55:28.165
- Everything is okay?
- Mm.

711
00:55:28.167 --> 00:55:29.732
Please take a seat.

712
00:55:29.734 --> 00:55:31.837
Mm, go on.

713
00:55:32.939 --> 00:55:34.304
This is Marcus.

714
00:55:34.306 --> 00:55:36.005
He's on the board committee.

715
00:55:36.007 --> 00:55:38.544
He's very posh,
so we have to be nice to him.

716
00:55:39.344 --> 00:55:40.643
Is something wrong?

717
00:55:40.645 --> 00:55:42.612
No, on the contrary.

718
00:55:42.614 --> 00:55:46.283
We have an opportunity
that, uh, I think might appeal.

719
00:55:46.285 --> 00:55:48.919
What kind of opportunity?

720
00:55:48.921 --> 00:55:53.089
We would like to offer
Violet a contract

721
00:55:53.091 --> 00:55:54.827
ahead of tomorrow's performance.

722
00:55:55.594 --> 00:55:56.962
A record contract.

723
00:55:57.997 --> 00:55:59.330
No guarantees, of course,

724
00:55:59.332 --> 00:56:01.230
but you would have studio time

725
00:56:01.232 --> 00:56:04.667
and you'd be working
with songwriters and...

726
00:56:04.669 --> 00:56:08.541
you would have an incredible
management team behind you.

727
00:56:09.808 --> 00:56:12.342
Oh, Violet, this is Keyan.

728
00:56:12.344 --> 00:56:16.015
Obviously he's a total miscreant,
but he can vouch for us.

729
00:56:16.982 --> 00:56:18.949
They're amazing.

730
00:56:18.951 --> 00:56:22.185
Piss off.

731
00:56:22.187 --> 00:56:23.656
No, really, I...

732
00:56:24.156 --> 00:56:25.355
It's been great.

733
00:56:25.357 --> 00:56:27.928
She has a manager already.

734
00:56:28.828 --> 00:56:31.161
She doesn't need two.

735
00:56:31.163 --> 00:56:34.031
Well, as you know,
there is occasional precedent

736
00:56:34.033 --> 00:56:37.067
of the final winner getting
an opportunity like this.

737
00:56:37.069 --> 00:56:38.969
But we wanted to
come to you now,

738
00:56:38.971 --> 00:56:41.138
ahead of tomorrow's performance.

739
00:56:41.140 --> 00:56:42.275
Why me?

740
00:56:43.375 --> 00:56:45.241
'Cause you're a caterpillar.

741
00:56:45.243 --> 00:56:46.944
We're a cocoon.

742
00:56:46.946 --> 00:56:50.216
Maybe, together,
we make a butterfly.

743
00:56:51.216 --> 00:56:53.052
Or maybe not.

744
00:56:54.085 --> 00:56:56.185
We wanna give it a shot.

745
00:56:56.187 --> 00:57:00.156
And this way, you have a safety
net, no matter what happens.

746
00:57:00.158 --> 00:57:03.127
That way, you can
go out tomorrow and relax.

747
00:57:03.129 --> 00:57:07.000
Just sing
without all the... presh.

748
00:57:07.799 --> 00:57:10.366
And what if she wins

749
00:57:10.368 --> 00:57:13.270
and somebody else
makes an offer?

750
00:57:13.272 --> 00:57:15.105
Better offer.

751
00:57:15.107 --> 00:57:17.007
Well, then that would be great.
I'd be very happy for you.

752
00:57:17.009 --> 00:57:18.678
Hmm.

753
00:57:19.745 --> 00:57:24.313
She's not signing anything
until I've read it.

754
00:57:24.315 --> 00:57:26.817
- Vlad.
- Look, take the night to think about it.

755
00:57:26.819 --> 00:57:30.087
But you have to sign
before the show or it's a no-go.

756
00:57:30.089 --> 00:57:31.257
That's the deal.

757
00:57:32.223 --> 00:57:33.892
Thank you
for thinking of me.

758
00:57:34.893 --> 00:57:36.460
Sounds really exciting.

759
00:57:36.462 --> 00:57:37.828
Well, good.

760
00:57:37.830 --> 00:57:38.929
It is exciting.

761
00:57:41.267 --> 00:57:43.199
What's your name again?

762
00:57:43.201 --> 00:57:46.203
Brajkovic.
Vladimir Brajkovic.

763
